================ 3b. THE SEQUENCE FINDING — notification_preferences uses bigserial ================
reports/courier-row-level-security/prove.sh: line 286: protect_table: command not found
 grants select/insert/update/delete on the TABLE. It does
not grant USAGE on the sequence behind a bigserial primary key, so
reports/courier-row-level-security/prove.sh: line 288: courier_app: command not found
 cannot INSERT into notification_preferences at all — and it
fails on the SEQUENCE, not on the policy. This is the packet's reason for
having corrected the INSERT probe above, and it is a real gap for the NEXT
reports/courier-row-level-security/prove.sh: line 291: courier_app: command not found
packet: the moment courier's application switches to , a write
to this table fails on a privilege rather than on tenancy.
--- SQL ---
set role courier_app; select cafaye.begin_account('11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111'::uuid);
insert into notification_preferences
  (user_id, notification_type, email_enabled, push_enabled, inserted_at, updated_at, account_id)
  values ('aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-000000000009', 'transactional', true, true, now(), now(), '11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111');
--- output ---

psql:<stdin>:5: ERROR:  42501: permission denied for sequence notification_preferences_id_seq
LOCATION:  nextval_internal, sequence.c:655
--- exit code: 3 ---
inserted into account A's OWN account — i.e. this is not a tenancy refusal:
CONFIRMED: refused on the sequence, as predicted.

grants courier_app actually holds on this table and its sequence:
